# 7. Command Selection Behavior

When the user selects an item using `/` or `@`, do not simply treat it as normal text.

The frontend should parse the command and identify:

```text
Command Type
    ↓
Feature / Assist
    ↓
Selected Module
    ↓
Backend/API Route
```

For example:

```text
/pms-assist
```

must internally resolve to:

```text
type: assist
name: pms-assist
backend: PMS Assist backend
```

And:

```text
@chat-with-pdf
```

must resolve to:

```text
type: feature
name: chat-with-pdf
backend: PDF processing/chat backend
```

Do not hardcode routing logic throughout UI components.

Create a centralized configuration/registry so that new features and assists can be added easily.

For example, conceptually:

```text
Assist/Feature Registry
    PMS Assist → PMS backend
    PST Assist → PST backend
    Chat with PDF → PDF backend
    Chat with Excel → Excel backend
```

The actual implementation should follow the existing project's architecture.

